# Tech Stack & Architecture

## Stack (all free for this assessment)
| Layer | Choice | Free tier notes | Why |
|---|---|---|---|
| Telephony + STT + TTS | Vapi | Free U.S. number (inbound works, outbound does not), ~$10 signup credit, no card | Handles phone, speech, turn-taking and barge-in, so we focus on prompt, tools and backend |
| LLM | Gemini via Google AI Studio, OpenAI-compatible endpoint | Free tier, rate limited per Google Cloud project (RPM + RPD) | Free, fast Flash/Flash-Lite models, supports tool calling + streaming |
| LLM access pattern | Vapi "Custom LLM" -> our FastAPI proxy -> Gemini | n/a | Lets us own the prompt in code, rotate keys, add fallbacks and log latency |
| Backend | FastAPI, Python 3.12 | n/a | Async, Pydantic v2 validation, auto OpenAPI docs at /docs |
| Database | Supabase Postgres | Free project; pauses after ~1 week of inactivity | Real Postgres constraints, external to app so data survives redeploys |
| Hosting | Railway (US East region) | 30-day trial with $5 credit | Always-on container, no cold starts, deploy from GitHub |
| Dashboard | Served by FastAPI at /dashboard | n/a | One deploy, one URL. No separate Vercel app needed |

## Python dependencies
fastapi, uvicorn[standard], pydantic>=2, pydantic-settings, email-validator, sqlalchemy[asyncio]>=2, asyncpg,
openai (used as the client for Gemini's OpenAI-compatible endpoint), httpx, jinja2, python-json-logger (or structlog),
dev: pytest, pytest-asyncio, ruff.

## Folder structure
```
app/
  main.py                 # FastAPI app factory, routers, exception handlers, startup/shutdown
  config.py               # pydantic-settings Settings, single source of env config
  api/
    patients.py           # REST routes only. No SQL, no business rules
    vapi.py               # POST /vapi/webhook (tool-calls, end-of-call-report, status-update)
    llm_proxy.py          # POST /llm/chat/completions (OpenAI-compatible, SSE)
    dashboard.py          # GET /dashboard
    health.py             # GET /health
  telephony/
    vapi_adapter.py       # Parse Vapi payloads, verify secret, format tool results. Only place that knows Vapi's shapes
  llm/
    key_pool.py           # Gemini key rotation + cooldowns
    gemini_client.py      # Streaming completion with retries/fallback model
    prompt.py             # Canonical system prompt, section-commented, rendered with date + caller ID
  services/
    patient_service.py    # create/get/list/update/soft_delete/find_by_phone. Used by REST AND tools
    tool_handlers.py      # Maps tool names -> service calls -> LLM-friendly results
    appointment_service.py
    call_log_service.py
  db/
    session.py            # async engine + session dependency
    models.py             # SQLAlchemy models
  schemas/
    patient.py            # PatientCreate / PatientUpdate / PatientOut + normalizers
    envelope.py           # ApiResponse, ApiError
  core/
    validators.py         # phone, state, zip, name, dob, sex normalization (pure functions, unit-tested)
    logging.py            # JSON logging, request id middleware, PII-aware helpers
    errors.py             # Domain exceptions: NotFound, ValidationFailed, DatabaseUnavailable
  templates/dashboard.html
supabase/
  migrations/001_init.sql
  seed.sql
vapi/
  assistant.json          # Exported Vapi assistant config (tools, voice, transcriber) for version control
tests/
.env.example
README.md
Dockerfile (or railway.json / Procfile)
```

## Layering rules (reviewers score separation of concerns)
- `api/` handles HTTP only: parse, call service, wrap in envelope.
- `telephony/` is the only code that understands Vapi request/response shapes.
- `llm/` knows nothing about patients or the DB.
- `services/` owns business rules and is the only caller of `db/`.
- `core/validators.py` is pure and reused by Pydantic schemas. DB CHECK constraints mirror the same rules.
- No raw SQL string formatting anywhere. Use SQLAlchemy expressions or bound parameters.

## Environment variables
| Var | Example | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| APP_ENV | production | `development` enables debug helpers like SIMULATE_DB_FAILURE |
| LOG_LEVEL | INFO | Logging level |
| DATABASE_URL | postgresql+asyncpg://postgres.xxxx:pwd@aws-0-us-east-1.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres | Supabase SESSION pooler string (IPv4) |
| GEMINI_API_KEYS | key1,key2,key3 | Comma-separated. Each key from a DIFFERENT Google Cloud project (keys in one project share quota) |
| GEMINI_BASE_URL | https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai/ | OpenAI-compatible base |
| GEMINI_MODEL | (fastest current Flash-Lite model) | Primary model. Check AI Studio for current names and limits on build day |
| GEMINI_FALLBACK_MODEL | (current Flash model) | Used if primary fails on all keys |
| GEMINI_REASONING_EFFORT | none | Disable/minimize thinking for latency. Drop the param if the model rejects it |
| LLM_TIMEOUT_SECONDS | 8 | Per-attempt timeout |
| LLM_TEMPERATURE | 0.5 | |
| LLM_MAX_TOKENS | 300 | Short voice replies |
| VAPI_SERVER_SECRET | long random string | Shared secret checked on /vapi/webhook and /llm/chat/completions |
| VAPI_API_KEY | ... | Only for optional script that syncs vapi/assistant.json. Never used at runtime |
| CLINIC_NAME | Maple Grove Family Health | Injected into prompt |
| CLINIC_TIMEZONE | America/New_York | Used to compute "today" for DOB validation |
| SIMULATE_DB_FAILURE | false | Test-only. Ignored unless APP_ENV=development |

## Gemini key pool spec (`app/llm/key_pool.py`)
- Load keys from `GEMINI_API_KEYS`. Log only masked keys (`AIza...x9Q2`) and key index. Never the full key.
- Selection: round-robin, skipping keys in cooldown. Prefer the least recently used available key.
- On 429 (rate limit): cooldown that key (use retry delay from the response if present, else 60s), immediately try the next key.
- On 5xx or timeout: cooldown 10s, try the next key.
- On 401/403: mark key disabled for the process lifetime, log an error.
- Max attempts per request: min(number_of_keys, 3) on the primary model, then 1-2 attempts on GEMINI_FALLBACK_MODEL.
- Retries only happen BEFORE the first streamed chunk is sent to Vapi. Never retry mid-stream.
- If everything fails: stream a canned assistant message such as
  "I'm sorry, I'm having a little trouble on my end. Could you say that one more time?" so the caller never hears silence.
- Guard shared state with an asyncio.Lock. Expose pool status (masked) in /health.
- Log per request: key index, model, attempts, time-to-first-token ms, total ms, outcome.
- Rotation is framed as failover/resilience, not quota evasion. Document that in the README.

## LLM proxy contract (`POST /llm/chat/completions`)
- Vapi's Custom LLM provider appends `/chat/completions` to the URL we configure, so configure `https://<app>/llm`.
- Verify the shared secret (accept `Authorization: Bearer <secret>` or `x-vapi-secret`). Log the first raw request in
  development to confirm the exact shape and headers.
- Build the upstream request by whitelisting: messages, tools, tool_choice, temperature, max_tokens, stream.
  Drop Vapi-specific fields (call, metadata, customer, phoneNumber...). Override `model` with our env config.
- Replace any system message from Vapi with our canonical prompt from `app/llm/prompt.py`, rendered with today's date
  (clinic timezone) and caller number (from the request's call/customer metadata if present, else "unknown").
- Stream back OpenAI-style SSE chunks: `data: {json}\n\n`, end with `data: [DONE]\n\n`.
- Ensure every streamed tool_call has an `id` and `index` (generate an id if Gemini omits it).
- If Vapi sends `stream: false`, return a normal JSON completion.

## Deployment gotchas
- Railway: pick US East (Vapi and Gemini round-trips add latency; do not deploy to an Asia region).
  Start command: `uvicorn app.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port $PORT`. Health check path `/health`.
- Supabase: create the project in a US East region. Use the SESSION pooler connection string (IPv4). The direct
  connection host is IPv6-only and often fails from hosting providers. If using the transaction pooler (port 6543),
  set `connect_args={"statement_cache_size": 0}` for asyncpg.
- Supabase: enable RLS on every table (no policies). Our backend connects as the table owner so it is unaffected,
  but this stops Supabase's public REST API from exposing patient rows via the anon key.
- Vapi: phone number -> assistant. Assistant model provider = Custom LLM pointing at Railway. Tools' server URL =
  `https://<app>/vapi/webhook`. Same secret configured on both.
- Testing from outside the U.S.: use the Vapi dashboard's web call ("Talk to assistant"). It hits the same LLM proxy
  and tools. Web calls have no caller ID, so code must handle a missing caller number.
- Fallback plan: if the custom LLM proxy is unstable by the 2-hour mark, switch the Vapi assistant to Vapi's built-in
  Google provider with a single key, keep the proxy code in the repo, and document the trade-off.

## Coding conventions
- Async everywhere. Type hints on everything. Pydantic v2 style (`field_validator`, `model_config`).
- Use the `logging` module with JSON output. No print.
- Domain errors raised in services, translated to HTTP in exception handlers, translated to spoken-friendly results in tool handlers.
- Keep functions small. Docstrings on public functions. Comments explain "why", not "what".
